{
  "dom_id": "step-e4388",
  "name": "Example: Determining the Dimensions of the Transpose of a Matrix",
  "problem": "Consider the matrix\n    ${B} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        1 & 2 & 4 & 2\\\n        4 & 4 & 1 & 1\\\n        3 & -3 & 0 & -1\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$\nWhat are the dimensions of ${B}^T?$",
  "worked_solution": "When a matrix is transposed, its dimensions switch from $N \\times M$ to $M \\times N.$\n\nSo, since $B$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix, the transpose ${B}^T$ is a $4\\times3$ matrix.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
